# Draft knowledge entry from ppp/2.5.2 issue #2118

id:                     E357
trigger_tool:           runtime|test|conan_test
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        Can't open options file.*No such file|unable to open.*(system|global).*(options|config)|--version.*(failed|exit)|--help.*(failed|exit)

severity:               2
category:               configure, testing, cli, daemon, fail-closed
match_keywords:         informational option,mandatory config,--version,--help,system daemon,global options,safe probe,allowlist,negative control,pppd
title:                  Allowlist informational daemon probes before mandatory global configuration loading

root_cause:             A privileged or system daemon loads mandatory global configuration before dispatching command-line informational options, so a packaged binary cannot answer version/help in an undeployed consumer environment even though those requests need no configuration, device or privilege.
affected_scope:         Native daemons and system-management tools whose pure version/help handlers are side-effect free but occur after mandatory host configuration, identity, device or service initialization.
verification_cmd:       Run the installed binary with exactly one version option and one help option, then pass an explicitly missing configuration file and require that operational path to remain nonzero.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           early-informational-option-allowlist
rec_description:        Before mandatory global configuration, recognize only argc==2 with an exact allowlist of side-effect-free information options; delegate to the upstream parser/handler so output and exit semantics are preserved, and leave every other argv shape on the original path.
rec_command:            Add a platform-guarded argc==2 allowlist before configuration loading, call the existing argument parser, then test version, help, and a missing explicit config negative control.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      staged-config-consumer-test
fallback_description:   If the upstream parser cannot safely dispatch information handlers before initialization, stage a minimal package-owned configuration root for the consumer test and document that the binary has no pre-deployment probe.
fallback_command:       Set the tool's supported config-root option to a temporary package-owned directory; do not write host /etc or /system paths.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          test-harness

forbid_1_pattern:       parse_args\(argc.*before.*config|skip.*config.*argc|--version.*in.*argv
forbid_1_reason:        Broad early parsing or substring detection can accept mixed operational arguments and bypass mandatory security or service configuration.
forbid_1_consequence:   A command that should initialize devices, credentials or network state can execute without its required policy input.

forbid_2_pattern:       echo.*version|printf.*version|stub.*--version|wrapper.*--help
forbid_2_reason:        Hard-coded package wrappers do not execute the delivered daemon and can drift from its actual version/help behavior.
forbid_2_consequence:   Consumer tests pass while the installed binary remains unusable before deployment.

forbid_3_pattern:       (touch|echo|install).*(/etc|/system).*options|create.*fake.*config
forbid_3_reason:        Mutating host configuration to make a smoke test pass hides the pre-deployment failure and can affect later tests or the device.
forbid_3_consequence:   Validation becomes non-isolated and may change system or network behavior.

principles:             P004,P005

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E214,E246]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

